---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import AnalyticsPreferences from '../../components/AnalyticsPreferences.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy and tracking information — AISEOOnline"
  description="Learn what SEO checks send to the server, how accounts and logs are handled, and the current analytics and advertising policy."
>
  <section class="page-banner">
    <div class="site-container max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1 class="section-title mt-4">
        Understand what a website check involves.
      </h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        This is a plain-language draft for operator review before public launch; it is not a
        substitute for a jurisdiction-specific legal privacy notice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section-space">
    <div class="site-container max-w-3xl space-y-7 leading-8 text-slate-700">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Information you choose to submit</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a public URL, the backend receives that URL, fetches its publicly accessible
        response within resource limits, and returns check findings. The optional AI generator may
        transmit excerpts of supplied text to a configured model provider if the feature is enabled.
        Do not submit confidential or personally identifying content.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Accounts and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Public deterministic checks do not require signup. Private account features, where enabled,
        use a Secure, HttpOnly session cookie and a short-lived CSRF token. Project ownership,
        hashed session tokens and verification records may be stored in the backend database.
        Production self-registration and private deep audits are not generally enabled.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Logs and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Hosting and edge services necessarily process network request metadata such as IP addresses
        to deliver and protect requests. Application logging and infrastructure logs may also retain
        operational data. The exact retention period, backup lifecycle and deletion procedure
        require operator review before collecting production customer data. Do not assume that a
        submitted URL or request is immediately erased from all systems.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        No live analytics service, ad network, advertising cookies or third-party measurement script
        is enabled by this source configuration. Aggregate first-party analytics is only a future
        opt-in capability and must be explicitly reviewed and activated before event collection
        begins. See the current preference status below.
      </p>
      <AnalyticsPreferences />
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Your requests</h2>
      <p>
        The project provides limited account metadata export and guarded deletion actions, but full
        private document and backup erasure procedures are not yet complete. The operator must
        confirm jurisdiction, legal entity, contact channel, provider list and retention schedule
        before replacing this draft with an operational policy. <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/contact/">Contact information and limitations</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
